# staging for hand-delivered design files; the files themselves are relocated into the tree
/files (*)/
/files (*).zip
# Real E1-E5 artefacts (2.5 GB). Deliberately untracked, not merely unpushed: five files
# exceed GitHub's hard 100 MB limit, so this cannot be committed without Git LFS. The two
# bridge gates in NEXT_STEPS.md §2.1/§2.2 read it when present and skip when it is absent,
# which is why a fresh clone sees them skip rather than fail.
/nn_results/
# Captured stdout/stderr from long training runs. Useful while a run is in flight (a
# buffered pipeline shows nothing until it exits, which makes a live run look dead);
# the artefacts that matter are under results/ with provenance attached.
/_run_logs/
# Packed training corpora (block_corpus_cache). Multi-GB int32 arrays that are pure
# derived data: every entry is reproducible from its key and its digest is re-verified on
# every read, so nothing is lost by deleting the directory — only the ~17-30 minutes of
# packing it saves. Never commit it; `manifest_sha256` is what proves two runs saw the
# same tokens, and it lives in the artefacts, not here.
/.corpus_cache/
# Scratch output from the throughput benchmark harness.
/_bench_scratch/
